WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.328
Welcome to Market Decoder.

2
00:00:02.328 --> 00:00:08.165
In the next two minutes you will see what a share is, how a trade happens in India,

3
00:00:08.165 --> 00:00:12.385
and why a share price and a business are not the same thing.

4
00:00:13.785 --> 00:00:17.352
A share is a small piece of ownership in a company.

5
00:00:17.352 --> 00:00:21.480
If a company has one crore shares and you own one thousand,

6
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.488
you own one hundredth of one percent of it.

7
00:00:24.488 --> 00:00:30.014
You share in what the business earns and what it is worth, for better or worse.

8
00:00:31.414 --> 00:00:35.982
In India you place an order through a registered broker.

9
00:00:35.982 --> 00:00:40.876
The exchange, NSE or BSE, matches it with an opposite order.

10
00:00:40.876 --> 00:00:45.525
A clearing corporation guarantees that both sides settle,

11
00:00:45.525 --> 00:00:51.561
and the shares arrive in your demat account at a depository, NSDL or CDSL,

12
00:00:51.561 --> 00:00:53.356
one working day later.

13
00:00:53.356 --> 00:00:56.374
This is called T plus one settlement.

14
00:00:57.774 --> 00:01:02.603
A share price is what buyers and sellers agree at a moment in time.

15
00:01:02.603 --> 00:01:08.369
The business underneath is described by its revenue, profit, cash flow and debt,

16
00:01:08.369 --> 00:01:10.748
which are reported every quarter.

17
00:01:10.748 --> 00:01:15.866
The two can move apart for long periods, which is why ATLAS shows both,

18
00:01:15.866 --> 00:01:18.028
with the date of every number.

19
00:01:19.428 --> 00:01:23.399
Prices also move in ways that are easy to misread.

20
00:01:23.399 --> 00:01:28.324
If a share rises twenty percent and then falls twenty percent,

21
00:01:28.324 --> 00:01:31.581
you do not get back to where you started.

22
00:01:31.581 --> 00:01:36.903
One hundred rupees becomes one hundred and twenty, then ninety-six.

23
00:01:36.903 --> 00:01:40.398
Returns compound; they do not simply add up.

24
00:01:41.798 --> 00:01:44.863
A structured research routine helps.

25
00:01:44.863 --> 00:01:49.630
Identify the security precisely, by its symbol and ISIN.

26
00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:51.674
Read the latest results.

27
00:01:51.674 --> 00:01:55.250
Check the date and source of every figure.

28
00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:59.677
And write down what evidence would change your mind.

29
00:02:01.077 --> 00:02:07.311
Market Decoder takes you through each of these steps with exercises and quizzes.

30
00:02:07.311 --> 00:02:11.052
This course is education, not investment advice.

